@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000

### 1. Create a fictional student
POST {{baseUrl}}/students
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "student_id": "STU-101",
  "name": "Jordan Lee",
  "date_of_birth": "2004-09-12",
  "email": "jordan.lee@example.com",
  "phone": "+1 555 010 1010",
  "course": "Computer Science",
  "address": "42 Example Street",
  "enrollment_date": "2023-08-01"
}

### 2. List all students
GET {{baseUrl}}/students

### 3. Search students by name or student ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/students?q=Jordan

### 4. List students with a course filter and pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/students?course=computer&limit=25&offset=0

### 5. Retrieve a student by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/students/STU-101

### 6. Partially update a student
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/students/STU-101
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "course": "Data Science"
}

### 7. Replace a student's editable details
PUT {{baseUrl}}/students/STU-101
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Jordan Lee",
  "date_of_birth": "2004-09-12",
  "email": "jordan.lee@example.com",
  "phone": "+1 555 010 1010",
  "course": "Computer Science",
  "address": "42 Example Street",
  "enrollment_date": "2023-08-01"
}

### 8. Delete a student
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/students/STU-101